cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "VeriDex: Structure-Aware Retrieval and Sentence-Level Verification for Question Answering over Statutes and Textbooks"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-22"
authors:
  - given-names: Swapnil
    family-names: Shukla
    alias: Swapnil007-Curious
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, India"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Swapnil007-Curious/agentic-rag"
url: "https://swapnil007-curious.github.io/agentic-rag/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An independent student research project: a question-answering assistant that searches a fixed,
  inspectable library of open textbooks and Indian statutes before answering, uses
  structure-aware retrieval, cites a passage after every sentence, checks each sentence's
  citation and numbers against the cited passages, and abstains in Grounded only mode when
  evidence is missing. Retrieval and attached PDFs run in the browser. The repository holds the
  ingestion, retrieval and answering pipelines, their evaluation on held-out test splits with
  paired bootstrap intervals, and the static web app with its rate-limited model proxy.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - structure-aware retrieval
  - faithfulness
  - abstention
  - citation verification
  - legal question answering
